      "claim_excerpt": "## Result\n\nThe package `research/p104-helper470-twin-rung-removal` edits the merged word of #5907 (\u03ba .003125282). It re-certifies the edited word with the chain #5907 used, which is PR #5827's own verifier, loaded unmodified apart from the declared pricing literals.\n\n- **Conditional \u03ba .003125804**, tested at .0031258090.\n- Exact raw crossing in (.00312581155791, .00312581155792), which is +5.2246e-7 above #5907's raw crossing (.00312528909884).\n- Paid bill: 66,852 \u2192 **66,834 calls**. Productive targets stay at 13,444 and the rank-mass surplus at 760.\n- Storage is unchanged: public inputs, owned fields, owned lifetimes and peak occupancy are 770, 29, 31 and 13.\n- The word has 22,803 events (#5907: 25,998; retained cap 26,000).\n\n## The edit\n\n- **The rung removal.** Helper 470's itinerary 3 \u2192 593 \u2192 714 \u2192 875 \u2192 1001 \u2192 131 \u2192 127 becomes 3 \u2192 714 \u2192 875 \u2192 1001 \u2192 131 \u2192 127.\n- **The source move.** Helper 704's chain 3 \u2192 593 \u2192 612 \u2192 127 becomes 3 \u2192 593 \u2192 714 \u2192 127, so helper 470 now reads 704 at frame 714. This is the twin of #5907's removal, where helper 468's frame-593 rung went and helper 703 moved to frame 712.\n- **The rerouted read.** Helper 560 no longer reads 704 at frame 612. Helper 268 used to receive that content through its frame-612 read of 560; it now reads 2\u00b7704 directly at frame 714.\n- **Four further itinerary changes:**\n  - helper 115 ends at frame 189 instead of 105;\n  - Y main 127's second chart is 595 instead of 602;\n  - helper 713 starts at frame 76 instead of 3;\n  - helper 736 starts at frame 749 instead of 424.\n- **Everything else** is a rewrite of the ordinary e",
