      "claim_excerpt": "## Result\n\n**Scoped proof in a formal register model (no new \u03ba).** For the four-role target `diag([A+P],[A+Q],[B+P],[B+Q])` of [PR #2085](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2085), extended by the fifth rational rank-one address `R_t = (1,t)^T(1,t)`, the exact minimum number of paid calls is **eight for every rational `t`**.\n\nAt `t = 1/2` this settles the seven-call case left open by [PR #2112](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2112): its `7 \u2264 min \u2264 8` becomes `min = 8`. It also answers #2085's open question for the whole slope family.\n\nProof outline (full proof in the package README):\n\n1. **Exponent support.** Expanding `\u220f (I+N_j) + [F_j]N_j` shows every monomial has exponent equal to a subset sum of the labels, as rational matrices. So each target frame is a nonnegative sum of labels with multiplicities bounded by the label counts. With at most seven calls, `R_t` can enter such a sum only at `t = 0` (exact enumeration over all rational `t`). For `t \u2260 0`, each of `A, B, P, Q` is therefore used.\n2. **Odd denominator.** `\u039b_t/\u039b` has odd order, so `L/2L` is the old lattice mod 2 and `R_t \u2261 A` or `0`. The #2085 rank/trace floor of 8 applies at every word length.\n3. **Even denominator.** `B \u2208 2\u039b_t`, and `A, P, R_t` give a basis mod 2. A word using `R_t` needs an even number (at least 2) of `R_t` calls, at least one `B` call by step 1, and at least 5 `A/P/Q` calls. The last bound is an exact minimum over all 65,536 masks. Total: 8. A word without `R_t` has the #2085 floor of 8.\n\nThe direct eight-call word attains 8.\n\n## Evidence and reproductio",
