      "claim_excerpt": "## Result\n\n**Scoped negative result, finite certificate in the raw-moment relaxation. No new \u03ba.**\n\n[#6030](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/6030) notes that removing helper 469's or 471's frame-593 rung is exclusive with #5907's and #6030's removals \"unless a new carrier of that content is added\". This package prices that route on #6030's published complete profile, using the raw crossing of `\u03a3 T_r r^(1-k) \u2212 \u03a3 P_r r^(1-k)` that this line bisects.\n\n- Granting a free third removal with exactly #6030's per-LOCAL delta again (\u00d718 LOCAL invocations) would move the crossing from (.00312581155791, .00312581155792) to (.00312633419236, .00312633419237), a gain of at least 5.2263e-7.\n- **One added paid call of any rank 1..145 defeats that gain**, whether it is added once in the complete invoice or once per LOCAL. All 145 ranks are certified in both settings: the crossing lands below #6030's lower endpoint.\n- One added rank-1 call alone moves #6030's crossing to (.00312167101310, .00312167101311). That loss is at least 7.92 times the free repeat's gain.\n\nA carrier can therefore help only if it adds no paid call, or if it earns productive target credit itself. This package does not price those cases.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\n`research/p104-rung-carrier-break-even/verify.py` uses only the standard library. Signs are certified with correctly rounded `Decimal` `ln`/`exp` at 60 digits and an explicit 10^-50 relative error allowance per moment. Positive controls reproduce #6030's published crossing and, with the stated delta removed once, #5907's (.00312528909884,",
